Two points deserve attention. First, the Basel Committee's June 2025 disclosure framework is voluntary, with adoption left to each jurisdiction \citep{bcbs2025}. Second, the economic damage function in Phase~V of the NGFS long-term scenarios relies on \citet{kotz2024}, a paper since retracted by \emph{Nature}; the NGFS states that only the GDP-damage variables are affected \citep{ngfs2025}. This study therefore uses the NGFS scenarios as a narrative frame and draws the hazards directly from climate projections.

