\subsection{Physical drivers}

Heat drives most of the change. At the loan locations, the average number of days above 35\,°C rises from \VAR{hot0} to \VAR{hot5} a year by 2050 under SSP5-8.5, and the hot zone moves from the south into the centre of the country (Figure~\ref{fig:heat}). The longest dry spell lengthens from \VAR{cdd0} to \VAR{cdd5} days and annual rainfall falls by \VAR{pr5}\,\% in the median (Figure~\ref{fig:drought}). For 2030, the three-year windows are dominated by year-to-year variability: one scenario even shows wetter conditions, which should not be read as a trend.

