\subsection{Sectors and regions}

Heat raises the score of almost every sector; drought then separates them, because the vulnerability weights make rain-fed agriculture far more sensitive to water shortage (Figure~\ref{fig:sectors}a). Relative to each sector's exposure, extra expected loss reaches \VAR{sec1}~bp for cereals and \VAR{sec2}~bp for olives by 2050 under SSP5-8.5, against \VAR{secres}~bp for housing loans (Figure~\ref{fig:sectors}b).

